<title>USA: Pulitzer Publishing Co Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>Pulitzer Publishing Co Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.82		    $0.75</p>
<p> Net			 18,110		   16,456</p>
<p> Revs		     151,943		  131,571</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  21,978		   21,845</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1996 includes investment write-down from a joint venture, resulting in an after-tax charge of $1.6 million or $0.07 a share.  </p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.62		    $2.26</p>
<p> Net			 57,500		   49,322</p>
<p> Revs		     534,088		  472,327</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  21,926		   21,800</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 includes one-time costs related to acquisition of Scripps League Newspapers, which reduced earnings by $386,000 or $0.02 per share in the fourth quarter and by $1.1 million or $0.05 a share in the full year.</p>
<p>1995 includes one-time income tax reduction, which increased full-year results by $900,000 or $0.04 a share.</p>
<p>Excluding one-time items, Q4 EPS were $0.91 vs $0.71, and for year $2.74 vs $2.22.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
